# A Supersampling if_ plugin for FreeBSD 
#
# Munin only polls every 5 minutes. This plugin samples the interface byte
# counters every 30 seconds and hands munin all of the samples, with their
# original timestamps, on each poll.
#
# Usage:
#   ln -s /path/to/ifss_ /usr/local/etc/minimunin-plugins/ifss_em0
#
# The first poll starts a background collector for the interface by itself.
# Nothing else needs to be started from rc.conf or rc.local. The collector
# is single-instance (flock on a pid file), so running
# "ifss_em0 acquire" by hand, or from an old rc script, is still safe; it
# exits at once if a collector is already running.
#
# State files are kept in $MUNIN_PLUGSTATE, or /tmp if that is not set:
#   ifss_<if>.pid    collector lock + pid
#   ifss_<if>.spool  samples waiting for munin (ts,rx_bytes,tx_bytes)
#   ifss_<if>.read   spool being handed to munin (internal)
